"Deep learning for CGI and visual forgery detection: a comprehensive survey | International Journal of Data Science and Analytics | Springer Nature Link (https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s41060-026-01192-9)\nciteturn213view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s41060-026-01192-9\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 331\nL0: Account\nL1: \nL2: 【0†Menu】\nL3: \nL4: 【1†Find a journal】 【2†Publish with us†www.springernature.com】 【3†Track your research†link.springernature.com】\nL5: \nL6: 【4†Search】\nL7: \nL8: 【5†Saved research】\nL9: \nL10: 【6†Cart†order.springer.com】\nL11: # Deep learning for CGI and visual forgery detection: a comprehensive survey\nL12: \nL13:   * Review\nL14:   * Published: 29 June 2026\nL15: \nL16:   * Volume 22, article number 211 (2026)\nL17:   * 【7†Cite this article】\nL18: \nL19: [Input] Save article\nL20: \nL21: 【5†View saved research】\nL22: \nL23: 【8†International Journal of Data Science and Analytics】 【9†Aims and scope】 【10†Submit manuscript†submission.nature.com】\nL24:   * 【11†Ahmet Korkmaz】  【12†ORCID: orcid.org/0000-0001-8706-7272†orcid.org】^{【13†1】} &\nL25:   * 【14†Mustafa Özden】  【15†ORCID: orcid.org/0000-0002-0362-4017†orcid.org】^{【16†2】}\nL26: \nL27:   * 146 Accesses\nL28: \nL29:   * 【17†Explore all metrics】\nL30: ## Abstract\nL31: The exponential advancement in generative artificial intelligence (AI) and physically based rendering has severely blurred the perceptual boundary between authentic photographs and computer-generated imagery (CGI). The primary purpose of this comprehensive survey is to critically evaluate deep learning-based methodologies dedicated to CGI detection and visual forgery analysis.\nL32: As our core methodology, we propose a systematic taxonomy that categorizes the existing literature into three distinct technical domains: architectural paradigm shifts (from convolutional neural networks—CNNs—to vision transformers), multi-domain feature representations (spatial, spectral, and color spaces), and multimodal fusion strategies.\nL33: A rigorous quantitative synthesis of reported outcomes exposes a critical generalization bottleneck: While state-of-the-art models routinely achieve > 95% detection accuracy in isolated, intra-dataset evaluations (e.g., DSTok, FaceForensics++), they suffer severe accuracy degradation under cross-generator testing and real-world compressions.\nL34: To overcome these critical limitations, this study identifies existing methodological gaps and outlines high-potential future research trajectories—specifically emphasizing hybrid multi-color space architectures, multitask learning, and the integration of explainable AI (XAI). Ultimately, this review establishes a foundational framework to guide the development of robust, highly generalizable digital forensic systems.\nL35: This is a preview of subscription content, to check access.\nL36: ## Access this article\nL37: \nL38: Log in via an institution\nL39: \nL40: ## Subscribe and save\nL41: \nL42: Springer+\nL43: \nL44: from €37.37 /Month\nL45: \nL46:   * Starting from 10 chapters or articles per month\nL47:   * Access and download chapters and articles from more than 300k books and 2,500 journals\nL48:   * Cancel anytime\nL49: 【18†View plans】\nL50: ## Buy Now\nL51: \nL52: [Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input]\nL53: \nL54: Buy article PDF 39,95 €\nL55: \nL56: Price includes VAT (Korea(Rep.))\nL57: \nL58: Instant access to the full article PDF.\nL59: \nL60: 【19†Institutional subscriptions†www.springernature.com】\nL61: \nL62: Fig. 1\nL63: \nL64: 【20†Image†media.springernature.com】\nL65: \nL66: Fig. 2\nL67: \nL68: 【21†Image†media.springernature.com】\nL69: \nL70: Fig. 3\nL71: \nL72: 【22†Image†media.springernature.com】\nL73: \nL74: Fig. 4\nL75: \nL76: 【23†Image†media.springernature.com】\nL77: \nL78: ### Similar content being viewed by others\nL79: \nL80: 【24†Image†media.springernature.com】